{"nodes": [{"id": "roadmap_roadmap_development_roadmap", "label": "UZCASTING Development Roadmap (single source of truth)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "roadmap/roadmap.md", "source_location": "header", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All project documents were gathered into /roadmap/ by client decision even though the spec asked for them in the root, backend/ and frontend/; the BACKEND_/FRONTEND_ prefixes exist because both architecture files would otherwise share a name. If the old Miro spec conflicts with this file, this file wins."}, {"id": "roadmap_roadmap_scope_exclusion_social", "label": "Scope Exclusion - Social Network, Messenger, Friends, Feed", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "roadmap/roadmap.md", "source_location": "SOURCE OF TRUTH", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The old spec carried a social-network/messenger concept that was not accepted as a core task; verified that no such feature exists in Cms/, Admin/ or src/adminpanel/."}, {"id": "roadmap_roadmap_message_entity_trap", "label": "Trap - the Message Entity Is Not a Messenger", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "roadmap/roadmap.md", "source_location": "SOURCE OF TRUTH", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The name invites deleting it as messenger leftovers, but it is the accept/reject reply the Telegram bot delivers to a casting applicant; deleting it means candidates never hear back, so a dedicated test guards it."}, {"id": "roadmap_roadmap_content_classification", "label": "Three-Axis Content Classification (type, category, genre)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "roadmap/roadmap.md", "source_location": "Kontent tasnifi", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Separated at all three layers - database, API and panel - and guarded by ContentClassificationTest, because the likeliest silent failure is someone folding category into the type enum, after which a podcast in the drama genre becomes inexpressible. The dev seeder had exactly that mistake: content types seeded as categories."}, {"id": "roadmap_roadmap_bunny_stream_decision", "label": "Bunny Stream Decision Pending", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "roadmap/roadmap.md", "source_location": "Bunny Stream", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The client added two Bunny documents on 21.08.2026 that define a fundamentally different video architecture - direct TUS upload to Bunny and signed HLS from Bunny CDN - contradicting the built local storage with chunked upload and Range responses. They also assume a different stack (Java 21, Gradle, uz.streaming, Vite). No video code changes until the client decides."}, {"id": "roadmap_roadmap_architecture_decisions", "label": "Architecture Decisions D1-D26", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "roadmap/roadmap.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Keep existing folders and stack, stay in JavaScript, introduce Flyway with baseline-on-migrate, money as BigDecimal, per-entity ID strategy, separate translation tables over JSON columns, optional per-locale media, dark blue panel vs spec palette for mobile, H2 file DB for dev, no enum check constraints in migrations, homepage assembled from cms_homepage_section, prices and rates in cms_platform_setting, and inline SVG instead of a chart library."}, {"id": "roadmap_roadmap_multilingual_architecture", "label": "Trilingual Architecture (UZ/RU/EN mandatory)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "roadmap/roadmap.md", "source_location": "\u00a73.1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Client requirement that all content and menus exist in three languages, with some images uploaded specifically per language."}, {"id": "roadmap_roadmap_bug_b1_unprotected_api", "label": "B1 - Entire API Was permitAll", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "roadmap/roadmap.md", "source_location": "\u00a78 B1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "SecurityConfig granted permitAll on every method and path, so DELETE and admin endpoints were open without a token and the written JWT filter had nothing to enforce."}, {"id": "roadmap_roadmap_bug_b2_personal_data", "label": "B2 - Public Endpoint Returned Personal Data", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "roadmap/roadmap.md", "source_location": "\u00a78 B2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The open catalog returned phone, email, exact birth date and body measurements, including profiles of minors - a legal risk rather than technical debt, fixed with a showcase DTO."}, {"id": "roadmap_roadmap_bug_b3_secrets", "label": "B3 - Secrets in the Repository", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "roadmap/roadmap.md", "source_location": "\u00a78 B3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Database password and JWT key were in code; resolved by gitignoring application.properties, shipping only an .example, and removing the JWT default."}, {"id": "roadmap_roadmap_bug_b15_paid_video_open", "label": "B15 - Paid Video Was Publicly Reachable", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "roadmap/roadmap.md", "source_location": "\u00a78 B15", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Media raw access served video without an entitlement check; images stay public while video now requires the right."}, {"id": "roadmap_roadmap_dev_environment", "label": "Dev Environment and Seeded Entitlement Accounts", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "roadmap/roadmap.md", "source_location": "\u00a715", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Backend must be launched from the repository root because file paths are relative; seeded app users cover the different entitlement states so access rules can be exercised without payments."}, {"id": "roadmap_roadmap_future_mobile_scope", "label": "Future Mobile Scope (\u00a714.2)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "roadmap/roadmap.md", "source_location": "\u00a714.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Watch later / saved items and other user-side mobile parts are recorded but deliberately not written now."}], "edges": [{"source": "roadmap_roadmap_development_roadmap", "target": "roadmap_backend_roadmap_backend_checklist", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "roadmap/roadmap.md", "source_location": "header links", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "roadmap_roadmap_development_roadmap", "target": "roadmap_frontend_roadmap_phases", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "roadmap/roadmap.md", "source_location": "header links", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "roadmap_roadmap_development_roadmap", "target": "roadmap_backend_architecture_uzcasting_backend_architecture", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "roadmap/roadmap.md", "source_location": "header links", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "roadmap_roadmap_development_roadmap", "target": "roadmap_frontend_architecture_admin_panel_architecture", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "roadmap/roadmap.md", "source_location": "header links", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "roadmap_roadmap_development_roadmap", "target": "roadmap_my_idea_master_development_prompt", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "roadmap